 to include large chunks of stock that would vest if, over a three year period, Apple outperformed two-thirds of the S&P 500, an index tracking 500 of the biggest public U.S. companies.&\nApple is up 31% in the last 12 months, and it's outperformed 81% of the stocks in the index, according to reports from Bloomberg and CNBC . Apple also is the first company with a sustained $1 trillion valuation , which it achieved earlier this month.&\nThat means Cook is lined up to receive a massive payday: 560,000 shares, the maximum amount possible, worth over $120 million at Wednesday's closing price of $215.05.&\nIf the 57-year-old executive is granted the full amount of shares, it will be the fifth consecutive time he's received the maximum payout.&\nCook's unvested shares actually make up the bulk of his estimated $625 million fortune. He currently owns 878,425 shares of Apple, worth about $188 million.&\nCook said in 2015 that he plans to give his entire fortune to charity . On Tuesday, he donated nearly $5 million in Apple stock to an unspecified charity, according to an SEC filing.&\nSEE ALSO:& Tim Cook donated nearly $5 million worth of Apple shares to charity\n This machine turns a truck into a tent in seconds - here's how it's installed", "external_links": ["http://fortune.com/2015/03/26/tim-cook/", "http://feeds.feedburner.com/~ff/typepad/alleyinsider/silicon_alley_insider?d=bcOpcFrp8Mo", "https://www.businessinsider.com/apple-1-trillion-company-stock-2018-8", "https://www.businessinsider.com/aapl-tim-cook-compensation-net-worth-2018-8#comments", "https://www.businessinsider.com/tim-cook-net-worth-apple-ceo-2018-8", "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2018-08-22/apple-s-cook-is-poised-to-reap-120-million-of-stock-after-rally", "http://feeds.feedburner.com/~ff/typepad/alleyinsider/silicon_alley_insider?a=LpSQB1pcmU4:X9wHdvfjodQ:qj6IDK7rITs", "http://feeds.feedburner.com/~ff/typepad/alleyinsider/silicon_alley_insider?d=QXVau8BzmBE", "http://feeds.feedburner.com/~ff